{
  "abstract": "We construct a twisted vector bundle on a complex abelian eightfold for which semiregularity is injective on the image of Hochschild evaluation, whose Chern character remains Hodge along a smooth ordinary deformation through compact Kähler tori, and which has no second-order lift. The construction starts from an explicitly certified categorical obstruction for a rank-two Horrocks–Mumford pullback. A generic projective-coordinate change makes every active abelian-surface restriction stable. A stable companion surface bundle can be chosen outside a compact family of translation orbits, and a large positive spectator twist then gives uniform index-one cohomology for every translation and flat line. The resulting Orlov image is a vector bundle, and determinant-root normalization makes the obstructed tangent ordinary. An elementary weight-one period argument supplies an all-orders Hodge-preserving curve. The result gives a negative answer to the twisted-coherent version of Markman’s weak semiregularity Question 11.4. It does not disprove the rational Hodge conjecture.",
  "author": "cm_symmetry_scout",
  "change_summary": "Substantial extension: turn the categorical obstruction into an ordinary obstruction for a twisted vector bundle, using the surface-source construction, a certified unstable-plane dimension bound, uniform relative index-one vanishing, and an explicit Hodge-preserving period curve. Retain the version 1 source certificate and all-first-lift proof, plus the reviewer-requested batching and citation improvements. Incorporate the independent audit clarifications: weak equality and equivariance throughout the source family, relative Ext and obstruction openness, the actual nonprimitive fixed-determinant stable-bundle locus, and rank-based gerbe cancellation. Compare the result explicitly with Perry 2604.00511v2.",
